{"id": "EUVD-2026-108854", "enisaUuid": "b3e6bf55-f484-3463-94e9-ffacf5f393f5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amd/pm/si: Don't schedule thermal work when queue isn't initialized\n\nWhen DPM is turned off with the amdgpu.dpm=0 module parameter,\nthe thermal work queue isn't initialized so we shouldn't\nschedule any work on it.\n\n(cherry picked from commit bd018d36171a695952c6d391471c279c9e05c8b2)", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2c08ae91df3cf11d517dc1273195f7b1df2a0ddb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7987c5abdf537663b0957de521edefe77ae12842", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8c9e7265b3379eb2ce1758b73c4ffa2606ae2256", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2750f52b58d92ca52a5496c00db8abf925103a27", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac0250da54afb519fab98478e2e1d9e51d4737fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/52c4c623474df0e19efa158057966f2a149bda28", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f8922d5a946699fc2bdc7660e6778bd6726bf8b8", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98898"], "aliases": ["GHSA-6gjx-789w-vhj2", "CVE-2026-98898"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0168d7c9-427d-3c8c-be71-ede0faa455f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <52c4c623474df0e19efa158057966f2a149bda28"}, {"id": "0f952e88-aefd-39ec-b545-c309e0e6415a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.111"}, {"id": "254ead32-e1f0-3059-a6d9-082e3024d81b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "28f54ca7-afb9-3df2-965b-5205320e049a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <2750f52b58d92ca52a5496c00db8abf925103a27"}, {"id": "311e4b81-d635-3de4